Use setuptools instead of the removed distutils.core.

asahi-fwextract's setup.py imports distutils.core.  Python 3.12 removed
distutils from the stdlib, so on Slackware AArch64-current that import works
only through the copy setuptools bundles.

setuptools.setup is the supported entry point: a drop-in superset of
distutils.core.setup that accepts the same packages= and entry_points=
arguments, and generates the asahi-fwextract console script from them,
without depending on that bundled copy.

--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 #!/usr/bin/env python
 
-from distutils.core import setup
+from setuptools import setup
 
 setup(name='asahi_firmware',
       version='0.1',
